{"task":{"id":"Prob133_2014_q3fsm","spec":"
I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input  clk
 - input  reset
 - input  s
 - input  w
 - output z

The module should implement a finite state machine with inputs s and w.
Assume that the FSM begins in a reset state called A, as depicted below.
The FSM remains in state A as long as s = 0, and it moves to state B when
s = 1. Once in state B the FSM examines the value of the input w in the
next three clock cycles. If w = 1 in exactly two of these clock cycles,
then the FSM has to set an output z to 1 in the following clock cycle.
Otherwise z has to be 0. The FSM continues checking w for the next three
clock cycles, and so on. Use as few states as possible. Note that the s
input is used only in state A, so you need to consider just the w input.
Assume reset is active high synchronous. Assume all sequential logic is
triggered on the positive edge of the clock.

","interface":{"top":"TopModule","ports":[{"name":"clk","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"reset","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"s","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"w","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"z","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false}]},"constraints":"SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."},"current":{"revision_id":"e35214ea-26bd-4e15-af49-521f42abf9dd","source_sha256":"2c90b7a83544ef28990a5e6bfa923389e47335c11faade785a42ec1cb7d4834b","source":"module TopModule (
    input  clk,
    input  reset,
    input  s,
    input  w,
    output z
);

    // State encoding:
    // A  : reset/idle state (only place where s is examined)
    // B  : first w sample of a 3-cycle group
    // C0 : after one sample, count = 0
    // C1 : after one sample, count = 1
    // D0 : after two samples, count = 0
    // D1 : after two samples, count = 1
    // D2 : after two samples, count = 2
    // E0 : output cycle, previous group did not have exactly two ones
    // E1 : output cycle, previous group had exactly two ones
    localparam A  = 4'd0;
    localparam B  = 4'd1;
    localparam C0 = 4'd2;
    localparam C1 = 4'd3;
    localparam D0 = 4'd4;
    localparam D1 = 4'd5;
    localparam D2 = 4'd6;
    localparam E0 = 4'd7;
    localparam E1 = 4'd8;

    reg [3:0] state, next_state;

    always @(*) begin
        case (state)
            A:  next_state = s ? B : A;

            B:  next_state = w ? C1 : C0;

            C0: next_state = w ? D1 : D0;
            C1: next_state = w ? D2 : D1;

            // Third sample: compute the final count = ones so far + w.
            // z is 1 only when that final count equals 2.
            D0: next_state = E0;                  // 0 + w in {0,1}  -> never 2
            D1: next_state = w ? E1 : E0;         // 1 + w in {1,2}  -> 2 iff w=1
            D2: next_state = w ? E0 : E1;         // 2 + w in {2,3}  -> 2 iff w=0

            E0: next_state = B;
            E1: next_state = B;

            default: next_state = A;
        endcase
    end

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset)
            state <= A;
        else
            state <= next_state;
    end

    assign z = (state == E1);

endmodule
